From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shi Jiayang <shi05275@163.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: yt922x: accept auxiliary VID 0 FDB notifications

A filtered bridge replays VLAN-unaware local FDB notifications as well as
its per-VLAN entries. VID 0 cannot be a data lookup key on filtered ports.
Accept these auxiliary adds and deletes without programming hardware, so
DSA can balance its CPU address cache without spurious -95/-2 errors.

Signed-off-by: Shi Jiayang <shi05275@163.com>

---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/yt921x.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/yt921x.c
@@ -6540,6 +6540,14 @@ yt922x_dsa_port_fdb_add(struct dsa_switc
 
 	if (!is_valid_ether_addr(addr) || db.type != DSA_DB_BRIDGE)
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+	/* The bridge also replays its VLAN-unaware local FDB entries while
+	 * filtering is enabled. No data frame can use hardware VID 0: access
+	 * traffic uses its PVID, and tagged traffic uses its customer VID.
+	 * Accept the auxiliary notification so DSA can balance its CPU cache,
+	 * but only program the subsequent per-VLAN entries into hardware.
+	 */
+	if (!vid && br_vlan_enabled(db.bridge.dev))
+		return 0;
 	hwvid = br_vlan_enabled(db.bridge.dev) ? vid : YT922X_BRIDGE_VID;
 	alias = br_vlan_enabled(db.bridge.dev) ? 0 : vid;
 	yt922x_fdb_key(addr, hwvid, entry);
@@ -6604,6 +6612,8 @@ yt922x_dsa_port_fdb_del(struct dsa_switc
 	if (vid >= VLAN_VID_MASK || db.type != DSA_DB_BRIDGE ||
 	    !is_valid_ether_addr(addr))
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+	if (!vid && br_vlan_enabled(db.bridge.dev))
+		return 0;
 	if (!br_vlan_enabled(db.bridge.dev) && vid > YT922X_BRIDGE_VID)
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 	hwvid = br_vlan_enabled(db.bridge.dev) ? vid : YT922X_BRIDGE_VID;
